Cheselden, William. 1728. “An Account of Some Observations Made by a Young Gentleman Who Was Born Blind, or Lost His Sight so Early That He Had No Remembrance of Ever Having Seen, and Was Couch’d between 13 and 14 Years of Age.” Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society of London 35 (402): 447–50. https://archive.org/details/jstor-103697.
